= Interventions used to Improve Health Outcomes in Patients with Multimorbidity: Protocol for An Updated Systematic Review
#smallcaps[Published]\ 22 April 2024

#smallcaps[Citation]\ #eval("Lim YW, Al-Busaidi I, Caya R, Bricca A, Wilson R, Mangin D, Abbott JH. Interventions used to Improve Health Outcomes in Patients with Multimorbidity: Protocol for An Updated Systematic Review. OSF, 22 April 2024. doi:~#link(\"https://doi.org/10.17605/osf.io/vypqh\")[10.17605/osf.io/vypqh]", mode: "markup")

=== Abstract
Multimorbidity has become a growing public health concern globally. The
aging population especiallyin developed countries has led to an increase in patients
living with multimorbidity.

In this study we will update a previous systematic
review to include studies published up to October 2023, with an additional focus
on economic evaluations of interventions for multimorbidity.

